.TH MEZZO 1 "October 2026" "Mezzo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mezzo \- privacy-focused front-end for Tenor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mezzo
.RB [ \-verbose ]
.br
.B mezzo \-version
.br
.B mezzo \-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mezzo
is a web server that lets people browse and view GIFs from Tenor without
Google's tracking and advertising systems.
It fetches search results, GIF pages, user profiles and media from Tenor and
serves them to visitors itself.
.PP
To view a Tenor link through a Mezzo instance, replace
.B tenor.com
in the link with the host name of the instance.
.PP
Mezzo runs in the foreground until it receives a signal.
It is configured through environment variables, not through options or a
configuration file.
See
.BR mezzo\-config (5).
.SH OPTIONS
Each option may be written with one or two leading hyphens, so
.B \-verbose
and
.B \-\-verbose
are the same.
.TP
.B \-verbose
Log debug messages as well as informational ones.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version of this build and exit.
.TP
.BR \-help ", " \-h
Print a usage summary to standard error and exit with status 0.
.SH LISTENING
Mezzo listens on TCP port
.B MEZZO_PORT
(default 8006) on all IPv4 addresses and on all IPv6 addresses.
It keeps running as long as it can listen on at least one of the two, so a
host without IPv6 works.
.PP
Mezzo speaks plain HTTP and does not terminate TLS.
To serve HTTPS, put a reverse proxy in front of it.
.SH HTTP INTERFACE
.TP
.B /
The home page, with a short introduction and a link to Explore.
.TP
.BI /search/ SLUG
Search results.
.TP
.B /explore
Trending searches and featured GIFs.
.TP
.BI /view/ SLUG
A GIF page.
.TP
.BI /users/ NAME
A user profile.
Tenor partner accounts use
.BI /official/ NAME
instead.
.TP
.BI /users/ NAME / KIND
A page that lists all of a profile's uploads of one kind:
.BR gifs ", " stickers " or " memes .
Partner accounts use
.BI /official/ NAME / KIND .
.TP
.BI /media/ HOST / PATH
GIFs, videos and thumbnails, fetched from Tenor through Mezzo.
.TP
.BI /avatar/ HOST / PATH
Avatars and banners, fetched from Tenor through Mezzo.
.TP
.B /static/
Mezzo's own style sheets, scripts and images.
.PP
Responses for GIF pages, search results, Explore pages and profiles carry a
.B Mezzo\-Cache
header.
So do responses for media when the media cache on disk is enabled.
.B HIT
means the response came from a cache.
.B MISS
means it was not cached and was fetched from Tenor, and stored if the matching
cache is enabled.
.B BYPASS
means it was fetched from Tenor and not stored.
.SH LOGGING
Mezzo writes log lines to standard error as
.IR key = value
text.
Under systemd they end up in the journal:
.PP
.RS
.EX
journalctl \-u mezzo
.EE
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Mezzo logs
.RB \(lq "shutting down mezzo" \(rq,
stops listening and exits with status 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Mezzo was asked for its version or usage, or it shut down after a signal.
.TP
.B 1
The configuration is invalid, the server could not be initialized (for
example, the media cache directory cannot be used), or Mezzo could not listen
on any address.
The reason is logged.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown option was given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run Mezzo on port 9000 with debug logging:
.PP
.RS
.EX
MEZZO_PORT=9000 mezzo \-verbose
.EE
.RE
.PP
Keep a media cache on disk:
.PP
.RS
.EX
MEZZO_CACHE_MEDIA_DIR=/var/cache/mezzo mezzo
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start the packaged service now and at boot:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl enable \-\-now mezzo
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/mezzo.service
The systemd unit installed by the Debian and Ubuntu package.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/mezzo.service
The systemd unit installed by the RPM and Arch Linux packages.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/systemd/system/mezzo.service
The systemd unit installed by
.B make install\-systemd
with the default prefix.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mezzo/
The README and the license.
.PP
For the files that configure the service, see
.BR mezzo\-config (5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mezzo\-config (5),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
